  "decision": "Held the $5K estimate at 64% and the $10K estimate at 34%. U.S. spot ETH ETFs added $121.1M on September 14 and BlackRock's staking-enabled ETHB reached $1.070B, strengthening the $5K institutional case without yet proving the broad, multi-year allocation required for $10K. ETH briefly traded above $2,600 but reversed to about $2,484, leaving market confirmation absent. Brent near $107, a 10-year Treasury yield above 5%, a firmer dollar, and roughly 93% Fed-hike pricing deepen the already-red cyclical liquidity regime. Revised CLARITY Act text is constructive but remains short of a successful procedural vote or final law. Ethereum's staking and tokenized-finance footprint remains large, while direct L1 economics remain too small relative to application fees to clear the $10K value-capture hurdle. No catalyst crossed a color threshold."
